In article <85652@lll-winken.LLNL.GOV> rush@xanadu.llnl.gov (Alan Edwards) writes:
>Anyway, I can definitely say that a potion of paralysis only holds the
>Wizard for a few moves, then it wears of and he comes after you as
>usual.  (It works that way for most monsters.)  Might as well just
>kill him.
A few moves is enough. The trick is to get the Wizard alive on an other
level than you. So you need not only a potion of paralysis but also a
scroll of magic mapping or spell of magic mapping. And the level should
not be a special level. In this case you need only a few moves to change
from level.

